<section class="blk blk--first">
  <p class="eyebrow">Contribute</p>
  <h1>Back the work directly.</h1>
  <p class="lead">Money is not the only way in — and right now it isn&rsquo;t even open yet. The most useful things you can give today are time, skills, and in-kind resources. Here&rsquo;s exactly what that looks like.</p>
</section>

<section class="blk">
  <p class="eyebrow">Status</p>
  <p><span class="status status--planned">Donations not open</span></p>
  <h2 class="sec">Donations not open.</h2>
  {#- SPONSOR-GATED: donations open only when a fiscal sponsor is confirmed. See records/SPONSOR_TRANSITION.md. -#}
  <p>Uncost is seeking fiscal sponsorship before accepting public donations. You can register an intention to give now, and we&rsquo;ll contact you when it opens — no money changes hands today. We can&rsquo;t accept donations yet, but we hope to be able to accept support soon. When we can, we&rsquo;ll say so clearly.</p>
</section>

<section class="blk blk--cream2">
  <p class="eyebrow">Three ways</p>
  <h2 class="sec">Three ways to back the work.</h2>

  <h3>Give — when donations open</h3>
  {#- SPONSOR-GATED: giving opens only once the sponsor structure is confirmed. -#}
  <ul>
    <li>Register an intention to give — we&rsquo;ll email you the moment donations lawfully open.</li>
    <li>One-time or recurring, once the sponsor structure is confirmed.</li>
    <li>When money does move, it is reported publicly through The Treasury.</li>
  </ul>
  <p><a href="/pledge" class="u-btn u-btn--ink">Register intent — sign the Pledge</a></p>

  <h3>Volunteer — time &amp; skills</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>The fastest way to move the evidence forward.</li>
    <li>Remote, flexible, credited in the public record.</li>
  </ul>
  <p><a href="/join" class="u-btn u-btn--ink">Tell us how you can help</a></p>

  <h3>In-kind — resources &amp; compute</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Compute, model access, and software credits.</li>
    <li>Equipment, data access, logistics, and storage.</li>
    <li>Reviewed in-kind support is treated as first-class — it lowers the cost of building Uncost itself. It never buys conclusions, coverage, or influence.</li>
  </ul>
  <p><a href="/contact" class="u-btn u-btn--ink">Offer in-kind support</a></p>
</section>

<section class="blk">
  <p class="eyebrow">Volunteer roles</p>
  <h2 class="sec">Where volunteers help.</h2>
  <p class="lead">Useful roles, right now.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Source &amp; licence review</strong> — check that every figure has a real, licensed, dated source before it publishes.</li>
    <li><strong>Data methodology</strong> — help design how costs are measured, compared, and refreshed by region.</li>
    <li><strong>Sector research</strong> — write and maintain a sector dossier: scope, opportunity, guardrails.</li>
    <li><strong>Engineering</strong> — build the open tools, and the data pipelines behind them.</li>
    <li><strong>Content &amp; design</strong> — turn sourced evidence into short, honest, shareable explainers.</li>
    <li><strong>Translation &amp; moderation</strong> — widen who can take part, and keep the community constructive.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Some roles may later become paid if funding allows. Volunteering doesn&rsquo;t guarantee employment or pay, and we&rsquo;ll always say so plainly.</p>
</section>

<section class="blk blk--ink">
  <p class="eyebrow">Start free</p>
  <h2 class="sec">Not ready to commit? Start free.</h2>
  <p>Signing the pledge is free, and it&rsquo;s the public demand the rest of the work depends on.</p>
